WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.500
CSS is visual, but learning it often feels disconnected.
A learner changes a line and still does not know why.

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:19.309
AI Tutor turns that gap into a guided experiment:
predict, observe, explain, and transfer.

00:00:23.548 --> 00:00:35.500
We begin with a real, self-contained HTML and CSS exercise,
imported into the visual canvas and rendered inside a sandbox.

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:47.222
Uploaded scripts do not execute. The lesson is in English,
while the current prototype shell is localized in Chinese.

00:00:52.979 --> 00:01:05.500
The purple brand color is declared once in the root selector,
then reused by labels, buttons, borders, and code highlights.

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:19.068
Surface, text, accent, and border colors follow the same pattern,
so the learner can inspect the page as a system.

00:01:25.810 --> 00:01:39.000
Now we open the source. The HTML remains unchanged because
the learning goal is theme control, not markup editing.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:52.002
In theme.css, global values are grouped at the top.
Components below read them through the var function.

00:01:59.771 --> 00:02:12.000
First, we change only the brand token from purple to deep teal,
then run a safe preview.

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:23.999
One edit updates every component that references the token.
Global variables make design decisions explicit.

00:02:32.245 --> 00:02:46.000
Next, we build a complete mint theme. Surface, card, text,
accent, and border tokens change while component rules stay untouched.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:03:00.980
The preview exposes the source, the learner's action,
and the visible result instead of hiding the answer.

00:03:08.730 --> 00:03:19.000
After the preview succeeds, we name the change
and save it as a new immutable version.

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:29.787
A failed edit would not replace the last known good result,
so experimentation does not destroy the learner's work.

00:03:37.054 --> 00:03:50.000
The canvas keeps both the original purple version and the mint version,
making the cause and effect easy to compare.

00:03:50.000 --> 00:04:04.260
The same approach supports box model, Flex, positioning,
and personalized lessons derived from imported pages.

00:04:11.035 --> 00:04:25.000
Versioned Learning Proof can replay course events, tutor messages,
tool results, fact receipts, and canvas saves on one timeline.

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:38.443
Machine tests cover the workflow and recovery,
but human learning research is still pending.

00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:49.500
Next, we would run a preregistered learner pilot,
complete localization, and validate on more devices and networks.

00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:58.811
AI Tutor helps learners see the cause, explain the effect,
and carry the idea to the next page.
